{"archetypes":[{"name":"manifest-schema-integrity","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The diff removes pr_number and status from manifest.json schema; verify no consumers still read or write those fields without the new schema, and that steps_ran dotted-key parsing in the manifest subcommand is correct under all edge cases.","prompt_body":"Inspect the manifest subcommand in scripts/larch-log.sh for the new steps_ran.<step> dotted-key branch. Verify the variable naming scheme (sn/var index arithmetic against args array length) is collision-free when multiple steps_ran fields are set in one invocation. Check that the immutability guard list still covers all fields that should be immutable, and that pr_number is no longer in the guard list (since it is removed from the schema). Confirm that consumers outside the diff (e.g. scripts that read pr_number or status from manifest.json) either no longer exist or have been updated. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"audit-map-runs-flow","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The primary/fallback lookup order in audit-map-runs.sh is swapped; verify the gh-failure path still emits an empty row and continues rather than short-circuiting, and that the manifest fallback is only reached when RUN_ID is still empty after the gh path.","prompt_body":"Trace the per-PR loop in .claude/skills/audit-runs/scripts/audit-map-runs.sh after the swap. When gh pr view fails (gh_ok=false), the code no longer emits an early-continue row — confirm that the loop instead falls through to the manifest fallback and then prints a row (possibly empty) at the end. Compare this behavior against the contract in audit-map-runs.md which says 'no manifest fallback on gh failure'. Verify the tmpfile gh_stderr is always cleaned up regardless of gh success or failure path. Check whether CLOSES_ISSUE populated from the manifest fallback path can conflict with a CLOSES_ISSUE that was already set by a partial gh path. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"steps-ran-gate-logic","focus_area":"edge-cases","weight":1,"rationale":"The steps_ran gate in audit-scan-run.sh uses jq -ne with --argjson to probe steps_ran; verify the jq expression is correct for the false/null/absent cases and that the steps_ran_obj parse failure fallback ({}) defaults to enforcing presence.","prompt_body":"Examine scan_required_file_presence in .claude/skills/audit-runs/scripts/audit-scan-run.sh. The gate reads steps_ran_obj once before the TSV loop, then for each conditional row runs `jq -ne --arg c ... --argjson sr ... '($sr[$c] == false)'`. Verify this expression correctly returns truthy only when the key is present AND equal to false (not null, not missing). Confirm that when manifest.json is absent or malformed, steps_ran_obj falls back to \"{}\" so all conditional files are still required. Check whether the jq -ne probe result is being discarded via /dev/null 2>&1 and the continue decision is made only on exit code — and that this is correct for the boolean-false case. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"commit-updated-at-race","focus_area":"code-robustness","weight":1,"rationale":"The commit subcommand now refreshes updated_at in-place on the source manifest.json before copying to repo; verify that a failure mid-refresh does not leave a truncated or corrupt manifest.json at the source path.","prompt_body":"Review the new updated_at refresh block added to the commit subcommand in scripts/larch-log.sh. The pattern writes to a temp file then mv -f replaces the source manifest.json. Confirm error paths (jq failure, mv failure) clean up the temp file and call larch_log_fail rather than silently continuing with a corrupted or missing manifest. Check whether the refresh also runs when src_path == repo_path (no-copy path) and whether that creates any double-write risk if the same commit call is retried. Verify the temp file is created under the same directory as manifest.json so the mv is atomic (same filesystem). Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
